## Finite coastline contract

Runtime exports **18** shoreline sprites: 3 morphology variants × 6 world directions. A coast tile deterministically chooses one morphology variant and uses it on every sea-facing edge. Review scenes use the same seed vocabulary; benchmark-only coastline morphology is prohibited.

## Host-side gate

```bash
python -m pip install -r tools/art/requirements-art.txt
python tools/art/run_gate.py \
  game/assets/terrain/generated-v0.3.2-r2 \
  game/assets/factions/generated-v0.3.2-r2 \
  --review-output game/assets/art-review-v0.3.2-r2.jpg \
  --qa-dir game/assets/qa-v0.3.2-r2
```

This performs:

- premultiplied-alpha Lanczos downsample;
- modular contact-shadow generation;
- manifest schema/current-source/Blender-pin validation;
- image/canvas/alpha QA;
- six-facing unit scale/anchor QA;
- decoded texture-budget estimate with/without mipmaps;
- complete wrapped color/grayscale/320px/75-100-125% review sheets.

Passing automation does **not** mark art accepted.

## Human premium gate

Create and manually fill:

```bash
python tools/art/create_quality_scorecard.py \
  --output game/assets/qa-v0.3.2-r2/quality-scorecard.json
```

Validate integrity/thresholds:

```bash
python tools/art/validate_quality_scorecard.py \
  game/assets/qa-v0.3.2-r2/quality-scorecard.json
```

Thresholds: every area >=9.0, average >=9.3, no Blocker/Major. A real Godot runtime-composition screenshot is also mandatory before visual lock.

## Source roles

- `vaelora_style.py`: immutable visual/runtime constants.
- `vaelora_contract.py`: semantic briefs + deterministic finite-library seeds.
- `vaelora_composition.py`: authored layouts/templates.
- `vaelora_materials.py`: procedural painterly material factories.
- `vaelora_geometry.py`: sculpted constructors and surface grounding.
- `vaelora_render.py`: master camera/light/render/manifests.
- `vaelora_artkit.py`: terrain/coast/Trama generation and source-context review scenes.
- `vaelora_faction_kit.py`: city progression + Basic Soldier benchmarks.
- `OPENCODE_PROMPT.md`: AI/MCP operating contract.

Do not duplicate these contracts inside ad-hoc prompts or scripts.
